A||||3||wwh0001||Oil Pan Leak||||5||
Z||000000||wwh0001||11-19-1999||08:43 AM||||I own a '88 Formula and a '87 GT. Both with the V6. The oil pan was leaking on the Formula a couple of months ago so I decided to replace the oil pan gasket. The Haynes Manual said take of the starter, remove pan bolts and the pan would drop free. WRONG. The motor mounts, exhaust and cradle are in the way. So after much wasted time I took it to a garage...Charged me $300.00 to fix.<BR>Now the pan is leaking on the '87 GT. The suspension on the '87 is not the same as the '88's. And it appears the pan will drop free.<BR>My question : will the oil pan on the '87 come off after the starter is removed?||||reg||5
Z||000001||sluppy123||11-19-1999||11:03 PM||||Unfortunetly no the oil pan will not come out after the starter is removed. The engine mount is in the way along with the exhaust.(I've done this 3 times on my 87 GT and I have it down fairly well)<P>First remove the passenger side rear wheel then remove the splash sheild. Remove the four bolts that hold the engine mount to the frame(leave the two bolts in the block there holding the weight of the engine) Look around under the engine for a place to put a jack to hold the weight of the engine(I used a bottle jack under the lower A/C compressor bracket) Take the weight off the mount, remove the two bolts and work the mount loose and out of the engine.<P>Next you can either remove the spring's that hold the exhaust in place or if you have an "aftermarket" cat loosen a clamp and pull the pipes apart(this will give you some play in the pipes so you can work the oil pan around the exhaust)<P>Then it's a matter of removing the pan and replacing the gasket(use the 1-piece rubber gasket and not the 4-piece cork & rubber one)<P>The first time I did this it took about 4 hours and the last time about 2.(practice makes perfect.............)<BR>||||reg||13
Z||000002||burdell1||11-20-1999||10:26 AM||||Is this the same procedure for an '85 V6 as well?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000004||sluppy123||11-20-1999||06:24 PM||||This should work on all 85-87 v-6 Fiero's. If you've added a rear sway bar it needs to removed also.||||reg||1
